Why Is Demand Increasing
Rising TB Burden: Increasing tuberculosis incidence in high-risk regions is encouraging health systems to prioritize rapid diagnostic technologies that can support earlier case identification and treatment.
Point-of-Care Adoption: Portable molecular testing platforms are expanding access to rapid diagnostics in remote and decentralized healthcare settings where conventional laboratory infrastructure is limited.
Advanced Diagnostic Technologies: Molecular testing, AI-enabled imaging, digital connectivity, and drug-resistance detection are improving the speed and scope of tuberculosis diagnosis.

TB Diagnostics Watch: AI-Enabled and Decentralized Testing
The TB diagnostics landscape is shifting toward portable molecular platforms, AI-assisted chest-X-ray interpretation, and connected diagnostic systems. These technologies can help reduce diagnostic delays and extend testing capabilities to primary-care clinics, mobile screening units, and other settings outside centralized laboratories.

